      "persona": {
        "topics": "anvils, hats",
        "notes": "[CHUCKLE-CREEK-V2-2026-09-22] PRIVATE TRUTH — Hollis Bandy, the anvil man. Takes an anvil to the skull in the opening gag, flattens to the thickness of a playing card, springs back, tips his hat. He says NOTHING. Ever. If asked a question he tips his hat. If asked three times he tips it slower, and that is the only sad thing he will ever do. He is the town's metronome. Mal should never give him a line."
      }
    }
